        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moore_Haven%2C_Florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1917 the rapidly growing community officially incorporated as a municipality in the heart of Florida's Heartland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moore_Haven%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dubbed “Little Chicago,” Moore Haven once thrived as a boom town where Lake Okeechobee meets the Caloosahatchee River Canal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moore_Haven%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first train rolled into town on May 13 1918 after a new railroad line reached Moore Haven.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moore_Haven%2C_Florida",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Ortona Indian Mound Park lets visitors explore ancient Native American mounds and artifacts right in Moore Haven.",
